  "notes": "Drawn from 2025-26 photos of A320neos (the A320ceos wear the same). A thin purple line edges the white nose's diagonal; a pale pink ring sweeps round the fin's lower half behind the lettering (only its run along the tail cone is drawn). Belly not seen squarely: the colors are taken to wrap under as the lower sides show. The far sharklet's inner face is white at the leading edge and magenta behind, the 'peach' lettering on it as on the outer face. Not drawn: the registration and type. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on JA216P (A320neo; drawnOn A320, the measured shape with the same fuselage): the wordmark's lowercase is 0.75 of its ascenders (type.xHeight), the fin's turned wordmark runs about 1.0 of the root chord, its baseline starting 0.4 back (at 0.08 the letters, which stand forward of the baseline, fell off the leading edge); the white nose's diagonal is a curve, now drawn smooth through its measured points.",
  "history": "Replaced Skyarium v1's approximation. Peach's only standard scheme since its first flights in 2012; the ex-Vanilla Air A320s were repainted into it after the 2019 merger."
